  "name": "mathlib",
  "description": "The Lean 3 mathematical library is a massive, community-driven formalization of undergraduate and research-level mathematics using dependent type theory. It implements a unified algebraic hierarchy and comprehensive theories in topology, analysis, and category theory, optimized for interactive theorem proving. Although succeeded by mathlib4, it remains a seminal artifact in the field of formal methods and machine-checked proof.",
